  "name": "Torviseitsikko (Finnish brass septet)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Finnish brass septet of E-flat cornet, two B-flat cornets, E-flat tenor horn, two baritones and tuba (the cornopean card stands in for the cornets and the credited-horns card for the tuba), first organised by Adolf Leander within the Guards' Band in Helsinki and from the late nineteenth century the common band of villages, societies and fire brigades across Finland, playing marches, dances and arrangements. Jean Sibelius wrote six pieces for brass septet, some for the Loviisa fire-brigade septet, and ensembles such as Sointu-Seitsikko, founded in Turku in 1971, keep the repertoire in concert and on record.",
